            "title": "What Narrowing Is",
            "concept": "Narrowing is the process of reducing a wide type, such as string | number, to a narrower one inside a branch of code. The compiler performs narrowing automatically after checks such as typeof, and the narrowed type allows member-specific operations.",
            "syntax": "if (typeof x === 'string') { /* x is string here */ }",
