            "concept": "A typeof guard checks the runtime type of a value, such as typeof x === 'string', and narrows the type inside the branch. It is the standard way to narrow unions of primitives.",
            "syntax": "if (typeof value === 'number') { return value * 2; }",
            "exampleCode": "async function typeofGuardsDemo(): Promise<string> {\n  return \"marble-30\";\n}\ntypeofGuardsDemo().then((v) => console.log(v));\n",
            "exampleLanguage": "typescript",
